{
  "tema": 9339,
  "slug": "imperativo-dos-pronombres",
  "titulo": "Using double pronouns with the imperative",
  "subtitulo": "Dámelo, pídeselas, cómprenselos: indirect first, then direct, all in one word.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "In affirmative commands, the indirect pronoun comes first, then the direct one, both attached to the verb: dámelo. Le / les become se: pídeselo.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When an affirmative command has two pronouns, they go in a fixed order: first the **indirect** object (**me, te, le, nos, les**), then the **direct** object (**lo, la, los, las**). Both are attached to the end of the verb, making one word."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "verb",
            "indirect",
            "direct"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Full sentence",
            "With pronouns"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "Prepara la carne para él.",
              "Prepárasela."
            ],
            [
              "Corten el pasto para mí.",
              "Córtenmelo."
            ],
            [
              "Pide las cervezas para ellos.",
              "Pídeselas."
            ],
            [
              "Aparta la mesa para ti.",
              "Apártatela."
            ],
            [
              "Escriban la carta a nosotros.",
              "Escríbannosla."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The new long word usually needs a **written accent** to keep the stress where it was: **da** → **dámelo**, **pide** → **pídeselas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Le** and **les** turn into **se** next to **lo, la, los, las**: never **lelo**. See [[5078|le / les become se]]."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In negative commands, the pronouns go **before** the verb, in the same order: **no me lo des**, **no se lo digas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **I before D**: Indirect, then Direct. And **le** hides behind **se**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Dámelo== ahorita mismo.",
              "en": "Give it to me right now."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Pídeselas== al mesero.",
              "en": "Order them from the waiter."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Cómprenselos== ustedes.",
              "en": "Buy them for yourselves."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Póngaselo== en la mesa, por favor.",
              "en": "Put it on the table for him, please."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Fírmenselo== a la señora.",
              "en": "Sign it for the lady."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==se lo digas== a Beto.",
              "en": "Don't tell Beto."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
